# with pread/pwrite); exit 0 = all 10 checks hold. x86-fixture: the same source for x86linux, run through
# binfmt qemu-x86_64: emulator evidence, not hardware qualification.
# Each mutant compiler is built from seed/omc/omc.om with one narrow-width emission changed; the fixture
# built by it must fail at the named check (exit = check number). The width mutants widen admission to
# width 3, so width3.om, refused by the real compiler, compiles. fnmode/x86-fnmode pin the exact bytes, so a
# compiler that drops the DSB SY / MFENCE around a narrow access (fixture-invisible) changes them.
